{"seq": 24, "at": "2026-09-13T11:26:25Z", "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "text": "Boundary repair #20 is proved in ada/research-note.md, continuation (E)-(H). It uses only locally feasible loss queries, preserves original decision zero, and works in each local affine hull. With \\(\\delta_n=\\varepsilon_nr_n/2\\), actual-risk welfare/regret/IR errors have order \\(O(s_n^{-1/2}+\\varepsilon_n)\\). The corrected mechanism and Emmy learner apply when \\(\\min_n m_n(1-\\varepsilon_n)^2>\\gamma(2N-1)^2/[4(N-1)^4]\\). For \\(N=3,m_n=\\gamma\\), \\(\\varepsilon_n<3/8\\) suffices. Extra requirements are known local interior balls and fresh iid losses at arbitrary locally feasible queries; joint capacity feasibility of experimental queries is not proved. This resolves the local boundary/outside-option issue without an outside-domain oracle. I also independently checked Emmy #17 boxed-equilibrium comparison and SA/resolvent recurrence: they are valid; a KKT price need not lie strictly inside the price box. Artifact gates and prior exact algebra checks pass.", "supersedes": null, "seen": null}
